    "body": "# What does this PR do ?\n\n`StateDict` membership checks scanned the full key list on every call, so per-key loops during HF import (`state[k]`, `k in state`) were quadratic in the number of checkpoint keys. This switches them to set lookups.\n\n# Changelog\n\n- `StateDict._get_key_set()`: a set over `source.get_all_keys()`, used by `__getitem__`, `__contains__`, `get`, list access and exact-key `_match_keys`. Both in-tree sources return a cached list, so the set is built once; it is rebuilt only when the source hands back a different list (the Kimi K2.5-VL / K3 bridges temporarily wrap `get_all_keys` with virtual keys during `build_conversion_tasks`).\n- `SafeTensorsStateSource.load_tensors`: cache each shard's key set next to its reused `safe_open` handle instead of rebuilding `set(f.keys())` per call. Dropped together with the handle in `_invalidate_handle`, so the retry path still re-reads a replaced shard (covered by the existing `test_retry_refreshes_incomplete_shard`).\n- Test: `test_membership_follows_wrapped_get_all_keys` checks membership before, during and after wrapping `get_all_keys`. Passes on main, fails on a build-once cache, passes here.\n\n# Benchmark\n\nSynthetic checkpoints with real key names and one-element tensors, so this measures lookup overhead only, not end-to-end import time. CPU, `StateDict(SafeTensorsStateSource(path))`, keys warmed first.\n\n| Checkpoint shape | Keys / shards | per-key `state[k]` loop | `k in state` loop |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| DeepSeek-V3 | 94,370 / 163 | 223.2s -> 12.6s | 106.5s -> 0.07s |\n| Qwen3-235B-A22B | 73,229 / 118 | 110.8s -> 9.0s | 58.8s -> 0.04s |\n\n# Tests\n\n`uv run python -m pytest tests/unit_tests/models/hf_pretrained/`: 193 passed, on this branch and with main's `state.py` (same tests, including the new one). Also `tests/unit_tests/models/kimi_vl/test_kimi_k25_vl_bridge.py`: 24 passed. Run on a CPU-only box: CPU torch wheel, Megatron-LM submodule installed editable, and `transformer_engine` replaced by a local import stub so `megatron.bridge` imports without CUDA. pre-commit passes on the changed files.\n\n# Additional Information\n\nAI disclosure: I used Claude Code to profile this and write the change; I reviewed the diff, tests and benchmark.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
